// Heroism: a touch-range spell granting a willing ally BOTH a temp-HP pool
// and immunity to fear in one cast. `SelfBuff` cannot deliver this -- that
// ability variant always lands its buffs on the caster (`entity: data.entity`
// in `common/src/states/self_buff.rs`), never on a touched ally. The
// established mechanism for "touch spell affecting an ally" in this engine is
// `attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup)` on a near-inert melee hit (see
// `lesser_restoration.ron`/`greater_restoration.ron`), but a single
// `melee_constructor` only exposes one redirectable `attack_effect` slot, so
// two ally-targeted buffs need two strikes. `ComboMelee2` with two quick,
// identical-range strikes is the smallest RON-only way to do that: strike one
// lands `Shielded` (the temp-HP absorb pool), strike two lands `Fearless`
// (fear immunity). Both use `damage: 1` (inert, matching the
// lesser/greater_restoration precedent) so the touch always registers as a
// hit without meaningfully harming the ally.
//
// `auto_progress: true` is load-bearing, not cosmetic: `ComboMelee2`
// defaults to requiring the input to still be held when strike 1's swing
// finishes (`common/src/states/combo_melee2.rs`) to advance to strike 2 --
// the "hold to combo" mechanic every real weapon combo wants. A one-tap cast
// (the natural way to use a support spell) would otherwise land `Shielded`
// and silently never reach `Fearless`. `auto_progress` skips that
// hold-check so both strikes always fire from a single tap.
//
// 🔴 `AttackSource(Melee)`, not `AnyDamage`, gates each `attack_effect`:
// `Stab`'s own `AttackDamage` entry is hardcoded to `GroupTarget::OutOfGroup`
// regardless of `attack_effect_target` (`common/src/comp/melee.rs`), so an
// `InGroup` (ally) hit always accumulates zero damage against this attack --
// `AnyDamage` (`damage > 0.0`) can never be true here and would silently
// swallow both buffs. `AttackSource(Melee)` doesn't depend on damage at all,
// same "trivially true for this delivery" idiom `septic_shot.ron` already
// uses with `AttackSource(Projectile)`.
//
// 🟡 Known residual limitation, not fixed here: each strike independently
// re-resolves its own `InGroup` melee cone (`attack_options`), so nothing
// guarantees strike 2 lands on the SAME ally strike 1 did if more than one
// ally is in melee range when this is cast (e.g. a second ally steps into
// range between the two strikes, ~0.7s apart). Low-probability in practice
// (single touch-range cast, sub-second window) but a real gap -- a proper
// fix needs a primitive that grants >1 buff from one melee hit (an
// `attack_effect: Vec<...>` instead of a single slot), not built tonight.
ComboMelee2(
    strikes: [
        (
            melee_constructor: (
                kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
                range: 3.0,
                angle: 20.0,
                attack_effect: Some((
                    Buff((
                        kind: Shielded,
                        dur_secs: 60.0,
                        strength: Value(15.0),
                        chance: 1.0,
                    )),
                    AttackSource(Melee),
                )),
                attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
            ),
            buildup_duration: 0.4,
            swing_duration: 0.1,
            hit_timing: 0.5,
            recover_duration: 0.2,
        ),
        (
            melee_constructor: (
                kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
                range: 3.0,
                angle: 20.0,
                attack_effect: Some((
                    Buff((
                        kind: Fearless,
                        dur_secs: 60.0,
                        strength: Value(1.0),
                        chance: 1.0,
                    )),
                    AttackSource(Melee),
                )),
                attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
            ),
            buildup_duration: 0.1,
            swing_duration: 0.1,
            hit_timing: 0.5,
            recover_duration: 0.4,
        ),
    ],
    energy_cost_per_strike: 20,
    auto_progress: true,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Enchantment),
        source: Some(Divine),
        // level 1 spell -> min_level 6, same `level * 6` convention every
        // other shipped spell follows (see see_invisibility.ron).
        requirements: (min_level: Some(6)),
    ),
)
